Theorem 5.7, 2464 random instances (|Y| <= 4 outcomes per run, up to 5 hypotheses, N <= 5 runs, lambda in {1.05,...,6}, 40% with the human in the class), all data sets enumerated; largest ratios of the two sides (must be <= 1):
  E[posterior mean of -ln A_(1/lam)] / rhs = 0.9578 ; E[-ln A_(1/lam)(MAP), worst maximiser] / rhs = 0.9578
  E[posterior mean of H2] / (rhs/(2 min(1/lam,1-1/lam))) = 0.6573 ; same for the MAP = 0.7034
  Theorem 5.5 (tempered posterior, alpha = 1/lam): E[posterior mean of -ln A_alpha] / rhs = 0.9578
